  "summary": "The health-tech landscape is shifting across several fronts this week. Conversational AI platforms are attracting significant capital, with Parakeet Health securing $10 million in Series A funding to expand its agentic platform for patient engagement, signaling continued investor confidence in AI-driven patient interaction tools. Meanwhile, the NIH is modernizing its public interface with a redesigned website aimed at cutting through organizational complexity, while questions persist about appropriate autonomy levels for clinical AI agents and the realism of broader healthcare AI visions. On the pharmaceutical side, Eli Lilly's direct-to-consumer model in Australia is disrupting traditional pharmacy channels, Pfizer advanced its vitiligo treatment toward regulatory submission with positive Phase 3 data, and a 340B drug program pilot is reshaping how drugmakers interact with providers through rebate-based models. Public health challenges remain acute, with Pennsylvania's measles outbreak claiming a fifth death, Congo's Ebola crisis now exceeding 4,000 deaths despite treatment center sabotage, and access improvements for addiction medications not yet translating into sustained patient retention.",
